.\" Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-sonnet-5-5
.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt JOTAIN-REVIEW-TOOLS 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jotain-review-tools
.Nd Emacs code review packages compared with repo-review
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This page compares the Emacs review packages with
.Pa lisp/repo-review.el .
The goal is a read-only review flow on Magit and Forge, for a whole
repository and for a GitHub pull request or GitLab merge request.
The data come from the GitHub API and from the git history of each
repository, read on 2026-11-16.
The MELPA recipes come from the MELPA repository, and the nixpkgs entries from
.Pa recipes-archive-melpa.json
of nixpkgs.
Maintenance states change; check the repository before you depend on a package.
.Pp
The criteria are:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The package never changes the reviewed sources.
.It
It works with Forge, or with a token that Ghub already stores.
.It
Every network call is a command the user starts, and the user confirms each write.
.It
It loads without optional packages.
.El
.Sh PACKAGES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy repo-review
The in-tree package.
It makes an Org queue with one headline per project file and opens each file in
.Ql view-mode .
Notes go to
.Ql org-remark
files beside the queue.
Dependencies are Emacs and Org only.
It reviews a pull request or merge request through Forge, keeps comment drafts in the queue, posts them after a confirmation, and has a viewed state and gptel commands.
It is GPL-3.0-or-later and in no package archive.
.It Sy reviewer.el
Repository
.Pa SreenivasVRao/reviewer.el .
A minor mode that annotates any buffer without changing it.
Annotations form threads and render to an Org document, for you or for an agent.
The last commit is 2026-11-14 and the project has 2 open issues.
It has no licence file, so the terms of use are unclear.
It is not on MELPA and not in nixpkgs.
It is young: the history is about 30 commits.
It requires Emacs 29.1 and
.Ql transient ;
posframe, treemacs and Projectile are optional.
It has no forge integration and no network code.
It fits the whole-repo flow, next to
.Ql org-remark .
.Sy Port ideas ,
do not adopt.
Port the Org render of all notes of a project, which hands a review to an agent, and the
thread model (note plus replies).
The
.Ql org-remark
notes of
.Ql repo-review
cover the annotation itself, and a second annotation layer would duplicate it.
.It Sy code-review
Repository
.Pa wandersoncferreira/code-review .
It reviews GitHub, GitLab and Bitbucket pull requests inside Emacs, from Forge or from a URL.
It uses Magit sections, Forge, Ghub and
.Ql emacsql .
Its last commit is 2024-05-29 and it has 66 open issues, so it is stale.
The fork
.Pa ag91/code-review
was active on 2026-11-11 and has 1 open issue.
Both write to the forge from the review buffer, and the package keeps its own
state in a database.
.Sy Skip :
the stale original conflicts with the current Magit and Forge releases, and the active
fork is a second review system beside Forge.
Port the idea of comments that stay local until the user sends them.
.It Sy github-review
Repository
.Pa wandersoncferreira/github-review .
It reviews a GitHub pull request as a diff in a plain buffer.
You write comments into the diff text and submit them.
Its last commit is 2021-10-11.
It supports GitHub only.
.Sy Skip .
Port the idea that a comment belongs to a line of the diff, which
.Ql repo-review
uses for its pull request drafts.
.It Sy pr-review
Repository
.Pa blahgeek/emacs-pr-review ,
on MELPA.
It reviews GitHub pull requests and, as an experimental feature, GitLab merge requests.
Its last commit is 2026-05-09 and it has 12 open issues.
It requires Magit, Magit Section, Ghub and Markdown mode, and reads its token from Ghub.
It does not use the Forge database: it fetches the pull request over the API when you
open it, so it needs the network for each view.
It is the best package for the pure pull request flow, with threads, reviews and notifications.
.Sy Skip
as a dependency, and
.Sy port
these ideas: one
.Ql FORGE-TYPE
setting for each host name, a pending review that collects comments before the user
submits them, and the Ghub token convention.
The
.Ql repo-review
code reads the pull request from Forge, which already has the data on disk, and it
adds the whole-repo queue that
.Ql pr-review
does not have.
.It Sy egerrit
Repository
.Pa eclipse-egerrit/egerrit .
It is a Gerrit client of the Eclipse project, written in Java, not an Emacs package.
Its last commit is 2022-10-07.
Gerrit is not a forge that Forge supports.
.Sy Skip .
.It Sy gptel-forge-prs
Repository
.Pa ArthurHeymans/gptel-forge-prs .
It uses gptel to write the description of a new pull request in
.Ql forge-create-pullreq .
Its last commit is 2026-06-24.
It needs Forge and gptel.
It writes a description, not a review comment.
.Sy Skip
as a package.
Port the pattern: build the prompt from the diff, call
.Ql gptel-request
with a callback, and show the answer for editing before the user keeps it.
The AI commands of
.Ql repo-review
follow it.
.It Sy forge-llm
Repository
.Pa rogs/forge-llm ,
self-hosted, on MELPA.
It does the same job as
.Ql gptel-forge-prs
through the
.Ql llm
package, and it uses the pull request template of the repository.
The host of the repository refused the network request of this session, so the
maintenance state is not verified.
.Sy Skip :
it needs a second LLM client library beside gptel, and it writes descriptions only.
Port the idea to read the pull request template when you draft text.
.El
.Sh COVERAGE
The table lists what each package covers of four parts.
The parts are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Sy A
Read-only review of GitHub pull requests and GitLab merge requests through Magit and Forge.
.It Sy B
Posting comments back as review comments.
.It Sy C
A viewed state for each file.
.It Sy D
AI drafting or checking of comments with gptel.
.El
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy repo-review
A: yes, from the Forge database and local git.
B: yes, drafts first, then one confirmed post.
C: yes.
D: yes, optional gptel.
GPL-3.0-or-later, in-tree.
.It Sy reviewer.el
A: no.
B: no.
C: no.
D: no, but the Org render is made for an agent.
No licence file, not on MELPA, not in nixpkgs.
Depends on transient.
.It Sy code-review
A: GitHub, basic GitLab, Bitbucket, partly through Forge.
B: yes.
C: no.
D: no.
GPL-3.0, on MELPA, in nixpkgs as
.Ql emacsPackages.code-review .
Depends on Forge, Ghub and emacsql.
.It Sy ag91/code-review
The active fork of the above.
Same coverage; not on MELPA.
.It Sy github-review
A: GitHub only, not through Forge.
B: yes.
C: no.
D: no.
GPL-3.0, on MELPA, in nixpkgs as
.Ql emacsPackages.github-review .
.It Sy pr-review
A: GitHub, and GitLab as an experiment, over the API, not through the Forge database.
B: yes, with a pending review.
C: no viewed state found in the source.
D: no.
GPL-3.0, on MELPA, in nixpkgs as
.Ql emacsPackages.pr-review .
Depends on Magit, Ghub and Markdown mode.
.It Sy egerrit
Gerrit only, written in Java, no licence on GitHub, not on MELPA.
Covers none of the parts.
.It Sy gptel-forge-prs
A: no.
B: no.
C: no.
D: yes, for the description of a new pull request.
GPL-3.0, on MELPA, in nixpkgs as
.Ql emacsPackages.gptel-forge-prs .
.It Sy forge-llm
A: no.
B: no.
C: no.
D: yes, for descriptions, with the
.Ql llm
package.
On MELPA, in nixpkgs as
.Ql emacsPackages.forge-llm ,
and the MELPA snapshot is from 2025-07.
.El
.Pp
A search of GitHub on 2026-11-16 found no newer package that covers part C or a mix of A to D.
.Sh RECOMMENDATIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy A (review through Forge)
.Sy Skip
every package.
.Ql repo-review
already reads the request from Forge.
.Ql pr-review
is the only package with the same scope.
It does not use the Forge database and would add a second review system.
.It Sy B (post comments)
.Sy Port ideas ,
done in
.Ql repo-review .
Keep local drafts and one confirmed post.
A pending review that the user submits as a whole is the open idea of
.Ql pr-review .
.It Sy C (viewed state)
.Sy Port ideas
from GitHub, not from a package, because no package has the state.
.Ql repo-review
keeps it as an Org tag with the revision of the file.
.It Sy D (AI drafting)
.Sy Skip
the packages.
.Ql gptel-forge-prs
and
.Ql forge-llm
write descriptions only.
The gptel commands of
.Ql repo-review
cover comments.
.El
.Pp
No package needs the owner's approval for a new source.
If the owner wants a second review system, the choice is
.Ql emacsPackages.pr-review ,
which is on MELPA and in nixpkgs.
.Sh CONCLUSION
.Bl -bullet
.It
No package gives a read-only, Forge-based review that also covers a whole repository.
The in-tree
.Ql repo-review
keeps its place and grows the missing features.
.It
.Ql repo-review
reads the pull request through Forge, lists the changed files in a queue, shows each file
as a read-only diff, and keeps comment drafts in the queue file.
Posting is a separate command that asks for confirmation and calls Ghub.
.It
Each file has a persistent viewed state in the queue file.
.It
gptel is optional.
The commands that use it say so when gptel is not loaded.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jotain 7 ,
